{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Text Generation Before Transformers \u2014 N-gram Language Models Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: trigram counts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from collections import Counter, defaultdict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_ngram(corpus_tokens, n=3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ngrams = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    contexts = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for sentence in corpus_tokens:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        padded = [\"<s>\"] * (n - 1) + sentence + [\"</s>\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(len(padded) - n + 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ctx = tuple(padded[i:i + n - 1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            word = padded[i + n - 1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ngrams[ctx + (word,)] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            contexts[ctx] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return ngrams, contexts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def raw_probability(ngrams, contexts, context, word):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ctx = tuple(context)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if contexts.get(ctx, 0) == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return ngrams.get(ctx + (word,), 0) / contexts[ctx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Input is a list of tokenized sentences. Output is n-gram counts and context counts. `<s>` and `</s>` are sentence boundaries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Laplace smoothing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def laplace_probability(ngrams, contexts, vocab_size, context, word):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ctx = tuple(context)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    numerator = ngrams.get(ctx + (word,), 0) + 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    denominator = contexts.get(ctx, 0) + vocab_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return numerator / denominator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Add 1 to every count. Smooths but over-allocates mass to unseen events, hurting rare-known events too."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Kneser-Ney (bigram, interpolated)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def kneser_ney_bigram_model(corpus_tokens, discount=0.75):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    unigrams = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bigrams = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    unigram_contexts = defaultdict(set)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for sentence in corpus_tokens:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        padded = [\"<s>\"] + sentence + [\"</s>\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i, w in enumerate(padded):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            unigrams[w] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if i > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                prev = padded[i - 1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                bigrams[(prev, w)] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                unigram_contexts[w].add(prev)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_unique_bigrams = sum(len(ctx_set) for ctx_set in unigram_contexts.values())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    continuation_prob = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        w: len(ctx_set) / total_unique_bigrams for w, ctx_set in unigram_contexts.items()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    context_totals = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for (prev, w), count in bigrams.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        context_totals[prev] += count"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    unique_follow = defaultdict(set)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for (prev, w) in bigrams:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        unique_follow[prev].add(w)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def prob(prev, w):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        count = bigrams.get((prev, w), 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        denom = context_totals.get(prev, 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if denom == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return continuation_prob.get(w, 1e-9)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        first_term = max(count - discount, 0) / denom"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        lambda_prev = discount * len(unique_follow[prev]) / denom"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return first_term + lambda_prev * continuation_prob.get(w, 1e-9)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return prob"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three moving parts. `continuation_prob` captures \"how many different contexts does this word appear in?\" (the Kneser-Ney innovation). `lambda_prev` is the mass freed by the discount, used to weight the backoff. The final probability is the discounted main term plus the weighted continuation term."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: generating text with sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def generate(prob_fn, vocab, prefix, max_len=30, seed=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = random.Random(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens = list(prefix)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(max_len):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        candidates = [(w, prob_fn(tokens[-1], w)) for w in vocab]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total = sum(p for _, p in candidates)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        r = rng.random() * total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        acc = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for w, p in candidates:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            acc += p"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if r <= acc:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                tokens.append(w)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if tokens[-1] == \"</s>\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Sampling proportional to probability. Always gives different output per seed. For beam-search-like output, pick the argmax at each step (greedy) and add a small randomness knob (temperature)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: perplexity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def perplexity(prob_fn, sentences):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_log_prob = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_tokens = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for sentence in sentences:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        padded = [\"<s>\"] + sentence + [\"</s>\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(1, len(padded)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            p = prob_fn(padded[i - 1], padded[i])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total_log_prob += math.log(max(p, 1e-12))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total_tokens += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return math.exp(-total_log_prob / total_tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Lower is better. For Brown corpus, a well-tuned 4-gram KN model hits perplexity around 140. A transformer LM hits 15-30 on the same test set. The gap is about 10x. That gap is why the field moved on."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Train a trigram LM on a 1,000-sentence Shakespeare corpus. Generate 20 sentences. They will be locally plausible but globally incoherent. This is the canonical demo.\n2. **Medium.** Implement perplexity for your KN model on a held-out Shakespeare split. Compare against Laplace. You should see KN lower perplexity by 30-50%.\n3. **Hard.** Build a trigram spell corrector: given a misspelled word and its context, generate corrections and rank by context probability under the LM. Evaluate on the Birkbeck spelling corpus (public)."
      ]
    }
